[x] Retire graphd and obsolete graph-runtime contracts =retire-graphd $After replacement evidence is green, remove the graphd binary/repository integration, subprocess bridge, platform gitlink, build/install/CI steps, and contracts whose only producer was graphd. Preserve historical decisions, portable SPARQL, ontology artifacts, and any responsibility explicitly demonstrated as still necessary; verify no Oxigraph dependency remains outside the optional CLI feature.$ !2 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-22T20:53 <migrate-graph-consumers #01a01834-5864-7272-85ca-919d45620a47
[x] Move the canonical RDF projection into Core =core-rdf-projection $Create an always-available clearhead-core rdf module using only lightweight RDF term and serialization dependencies. Move and reconcile graphd's domain-to-RDF and canonical JSON-LD logic so one dataset projection owns all triples, named graphs, stable IRIs, datatypes, deterministic ordering, validation, and every RDF serialization. JSON-LD must serialize the same canonical dataset rather than remain a parallel hand-built graph path. Keep Oxigraph, SPARQL, persistence, networking, and presentation out of Core; prove the normal dependency graph remains database-free.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-22T21:08 <rdf-dataset-contract #01a01834-581e-70f0-a4c7-0a499ebe4a19
[x] Expose whole-workspace RDF export from the CLI =cli-rdf-export $Add an always-available clearhead export workspace interface over Core's projection. Support dataset-preserving TriG and N-Quads plus the retained JSON-LD or graph-only formats whose semantics are explicit; cover workspace selection, stdout and output files, empty datasets, deterministic bytes, failures, and broken pipes without duplicating semantic mapping in the CLI.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-22T21:08 <core-rdf-projection #01a01834-582c-7321-b77c-4986f79793b0
